---
description: Naming conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

- Route segments are kebab-case. Next.js special files keep their required names.
- Components are PascalCase. Hooks start with `use`.
- Booleans start with `is`, `has`, `can`, or `should`. Functions start with a verb.
- Props interfaces use an `I` prefix only when a named interface is clearer than an inline type. Domain types use a `T` prefix.
- Use `E` prefixes for const objects that model a closed set, such as `EAppRoutes` and `EUserRole`.
- App paths live in `EAppRoutes`. API paths live in `EApiRoutes`. Do not hard-code those strings in components or hooks.
- Style modules are named `Component.style.ts` when a component's styles leave the JSX.
